{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Five cattle, etc.</b> Rabbi Yochanan ben Zakkai said: the Omnipresent was mindful of the dignity of creatures — an ox that walks on its legs and in which the thief was not degraded by carrying it on his shoulder, he pays five; a sheep, which he carries on his shoulder, he pays four, since he was degraded in it. Rabbi Meir said: come and see how great is the power of labor — an ox, whose labor he deprived him of, five; a sheep, whose labor he did not deprive him of, four (Mekhilta; Bava Kama 79)." "<b>In place of the ox, in place of the sheep.</b> Scripture repeated, to tell you that the law of fourfold and fivefold payment applies only to an ox and a sheep alone (Bava Kama 67)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:45.991240738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}